diff --git a/docs/MUSE-COMPATIBILITY.md b/docs/MUSE-COMPATIBILITY.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a8f61f8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/MUSE-COMPATIBILITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Muse 1.2.8 compatibility candidate
+
+This local candidate is based on dsh-purge Community 1.6.86. It targets the inspected Muse 1.2.8 runtime (DSH 0.2.1-alpha.1 and Cordis 4.0.5-alpha.1). It does not qualify other alpha builds or future Muse releases.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Add a precise SystemPrompt patch variant for the shipped Muse implementation, preserving context suppression and existing tool/variable behavior.
+- Preserve Muse's own update coordinator and verified native shutdown behavior. These DSH shell patches are reported as not applicable, not as applied.
+- Select Windows restart targets by full executable path and creation identity; reject ambiguous or stale process identities.
+- Avoid repeated header/hook edits when patches are applied again.
+- Keep original and applied file identities for backup and rollback; report unknown changes instead of silently adopting them.
+
+The original upstream license and notices remain in this package. Local adaptation files are identified in the accompanying build manifest.
+
+## Validation
+
+The adaptation tests cover real Cordis/SystemPrompt services, native shutdown behavior, two Windows process instances, repeated patch application, backup identity, and rollback. Full-host integration also compares the original bytes after reverting every target file and checks the generated JavaScript syntax.
+
+Passing these checks does not establish any guarantee about model responses, all external services, or video quality. Production scene, subtitle, audio, payment and delivery checks remain separate Muse responsibilities.
+
+## Installation and updates
+
+Use the isolated candidate first. Its profile, temporary directories and Electron user data must be separate from the regular installation. Do not enable automatic upstream replacement of this local adaptation. A later upstream package or Muse runtime requires renewed compatibility tests.
+
+Do not load an old dsh-purge alongside this package. Existing capability differences must be reviewed individually rather than double-registering hooks and commands.
+
+Local desktop loading, frontend/backend version alignment, forced restart and session retention have been checked. User acceptance is pending. The generic installer path from a sealed third-party archive has not been qualified by this extracted-host test. This candidate has not been submitted or merged into the production Muse repository.
